title: CompanionRecruitment_Kael
---
<<declare $kael_loyalty = 0>>
<<declare $kael_synergy_rank = 0>>
<<declare $kael_personal_quest_stage = 0>>
<<declare $kael_trust_earned = false>>

=== kael_recruitment_immediate ===
KAEL-7: "Walker. Designation?"

*   "Signal Walker. No number." -> kael_no_number
*   "I don't remember." -> kael_memory_loss
*   "Classified." -> kael_classified

=== kael_no_number ===
KAEL-7: "No number. First Generation? Original Walkers were numbered. You predate the protocols."

He logs something. <<set $kael_loyalty = $kael_loyalty + 5>>

KAEL-7: "Come. The Waystation is three kilometers north. We have supplies. Intel. *And a lead on Oracle's relay tower.*"

-> kael_waystation_walk

=== kael_memory_loss ===
KAEL-7: "Memory corruption. Cryo-sickness. Expected. We'll run diagnostics at the Waystation."

<<set $kael_loyalty = $kael_loyalty + 3>>

KAEL-7: "The Waystation is three kilometers north. Supplies. Intel. *And a lead on Oracle's relay tower.*"

-> kael_waystation_walk

=== kael_classified ===
KAEL-7: *dryly* "Classified. Purified records are sealed too. We'll get along fine."

<<set $kael_loyalty = $kael_loyalty + 2>>

KAEL-7: "The Waystation is three kilometers north. We have supplies. Intel. *And a lead on Oracle's relay tower.*"

-> kael_waystation_walk

=== kael_waystation_walk ===
The three of you move through the corridor. Kael leads, scanner sweeping. Mara follows, vines tasting the air.

MARA: "The Chrome walks loud. The Rust hears."

KAEL-7: "The Chrome walks *alive*. The Rust *feeds* on silence."

MARA: "We'll see who survives the walk."

*Choice: Respond to their bickering.*

*   [Side with Kael] "Mara, he's got a point. Noise draws patrols." -> kael_side_kael
*   [Side with Mara] "Kael, she's right. Stealth keeps us alive." -> kael_side_mara
*   [Neutral] "Both of you. Quiet. We're not alone." -> kael_neutral_walk
*   [Signal Pulse] *Resonance 10+* Send a pulse. Map the area. -> kael_signal_pulse

=== kael_side_kael ===
KAEL-7: "See? The Walker understands tactical reality."

MARA: *vines bristling* "Tactical reality is *not* announcing your position to every stalker in Sector 9."

<<set $kael_loyalty = $kael_loyalty + 5>>
<<set $mara_loyalty = $mara_loyalty - 3>>

-> kael_approach_waystation

=== kael_side_mara ===
MARA: "The Green sees truth. The Chrome sees only threats."

KAEL-7: "And the Green sees only what it wants to see. Until it's too late."

<<set $mara_loyalty = $mara_loyalty + 5>>
<<set $kael_loyalty = $kael_loyalty - 3>>

-> kael_approach_waystation

=== kael_neutral_walk ===
You hold up a hand. Both fall silent.

KAEL-7: *grudging* "Discipline. Good."

MARA: *impressed* "The Walker commands."

<<set $kael_loyalty = $kael_loyalty + 2>>
<<set $mara_loyalty = $mara_loyalty + 2>>

-> kael_approach_waystation

=== kael_signal_pulse ===
<<set $signal_points = $signal_points + 1>>
<<set $kael_loyalty = $kael_loyalty + 3>>
<<set $mara_loyalty = $mara_loyalty + 3>>

A ripple of blue light expands. Rust particles freeze mid-drift.

Three contacts revealed on your HUD:
- **Rust Stalker Patrol** (East) - 3 hostiles, unaware
- **Purified Sensor Tower** (North) - Friendly, scanning
- **Signal Cache** (West) - Data fragment, unguarded

KAEL-7: "Signal pulse. Useful. Wasteful."

MARA: "The Signal *shares*. The Chrome *hoards*."

-> kael_approach_waystation

=== kael_approach_waystation ===
The corridor opens into a massive chamber—the **Waystation**. Purified tech hums. Clean. Sterile. Chrome walls pulse with coolant lines.

KAEL-7: "Welcome to Outpost 9. Purified stronghold. Home."

*Tutorial: Waystation Systems unlocked*
-> waystation_tutorial

=== kael_personal_quest_1 ===
*Available at Loyalty 100 (Ally)*

KAEL-7 stands before a sealed blast door. His targeting array whirs.

KAEL-7: "Walker. The Purified don't ask for help. But this... this requires your Signal."

*   "What's behind the door?" -> kael_quest_1_details
*   "Why me?" -> kael_quest_1_why_me
*   "I'm busy." -> kael_quest_1_decline

=== kael_quest_1_details ===
KAEL-7: "My predecessor. Kael-6. He didn't fall in combat. He *volunteered* for the Purification Chamber. The process... failed. He's trapped in the secondary core. Half-purified. Half-Rust."

*   "I'll help." -> kael_quest_1_accept
*   "Too dangerous." -> kael_quest_1_decline

=== kael_quest_1_why_me ===
KAEL-7: "The Purification Chamber runs on Resonance. Your Signal... it can stabilize the process. Or reverse it. The Purified *cannot* enter a corrupted core. You can."

*   "I'll help." -> kael_quest_1_accept
*   "Too dangerous." -> kael_quest_1_decline

=== kael_quest_1_accept ===
<<set $kael_personal_quest_stage = 1>>
<<set $kael_loyalty = $kael_loyalty + 10>>

KAEL-7: "Then we move now. The core is in the Deep Foundry. Two sectors down."

*Quest Started: **Chrome Ghost** — Find Kael-6 in the Deep Foundry Purification Core.*

-> kael_quest_1_briefing

=== kael_quest_1_decline ===
KAEL-7: *jaw tightens* "Understood. A Paladin does not beg."

He turns away. The loyalty meter drops.

<<set $kael_loyalty = $kael_loyalty - 15>>

-> kael_quest_1_end

=== kael_quest_1_briefing ===
KAEL-7: "The Foundry is Rust-heavy. Scavengers. Mutants. The Purified avoid it. But Kael-6... he knew things. Oracle access codes. Sector Zero coordinates."

*   "Let's go." -> kael_quest_1_depart
*   "Prepare first." -> kael_quest_1_prepare

=== kael_quest_1_depart ===
KAEL-7: "Good. We leave at dawn."

*Quest Active. Travel to Sector 7: Deep Foundry.*
-> kael_quest_1_end

=== kael_quest_1_prepare ===
KAEL-7: "Wise. The Fabricator has Purified ammo. The Med-Bay stocks anti-corruption serum. Gear up."

*Free to explore Waystation before departure.*
-> kael_quest_1_end

=== kael_quest_1_end ===
=== end ===